    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1156">

                <pb facs="1005" n="901" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg901"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/38.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Chargé d’Affaires.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1462.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-11-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 10, 1913.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 2099,
                    of October 20, transmitting two notes from your Spanish colleague in regard to
                    the recent outrages against Spaniards in northern Mexico.</p>
                <p>In reply you are instructed to say to the Spanish Minister that the Department
                    has made representations which it is hoped will result in the protection of
                    Spanish subjects in Mexico and in the punishment of those persons who have
                    committed the outrages referred to.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
